  "semantics": {
    "request": "Exact Request identity at the first eligible portfolio-preview HTTP boundary, after original route/mode guards and before body/admit; entry does not prove authorization or producer entry.",
    "units": "Each entered port/compare unit retains its own ordinal and explicit parent unit/phase from the captured private ALS token; no ambient last-unit association.",
    "phaseEntry": "Boundary reached before the original callee lookup/receiver/argument evaluation. It is not proof that a callee started or an awaited operation is blocked.",
    "phaseClose": "returned only at the post-await identity tap; abrupt is a synchronous expression failure; rejected follows an awaited rejection; abandoned means that no return/rejection of that phase was established.",
    "concurrent": "Unit catch/finally closes only its own active phase. Pending siblings remain open; nested/concurrent durations are never exclusive or additive.",
    "scope": "Missing or foreign tokens use a neutral private scope. Mechanism faults or failed exact installation disable attribution permanently before work/fallback; no reselection.",
    "terminal": "request-close records boundary outcome and pre-terminal transport flags. It cannot attest its own output, subsequent fsync/close, all unit completion, or an untruncated trace.",
    "partial": "Killed/aborted process or I/O failure may leave only a prefix, a partial trailing line, or no stream. No terminal is fabricated. Entries can survive without a unit close.",
    "overflow": "A full successful comparison can use many phases; the bounded prefix is deliberately allowed to truncate before the journey ends. This is not a promise that all comparisons fit.",
    "clock": "Only server performance.now, in integer tenths of milliseconds from selection. Invalid/backward clock yields null plus clockFault; no comparison with browser/runtime-report UTC clocks.",
    "errors": "Observer errors are contained; product work result/Promise identity and exact thrown value, including undefined, remain authoritative.",
    "io": "One file write and one stdout attempt per admitted row; write(false) is recorded as backpressure and is never retried. Failed/partial file writes stop file appends. fsync/fstat/close only at request-close."
